\name{cellucid_history_group_create}
\alias{cellucid_history_group_create}
\title{Group steps}
\usage{
cellucid_history_group_create(viewer, from, to, name)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{from}{Its first step. Text. Required.}
\item{to}{Its last step. Text. Required.}
\item{name}{A name, unique among its kind (compared without case and extra spaces); no length limit. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{group}, \code{journal} (Its Recently changed entry), \code{steps} (Steps in it).
}
\description{
Name a run of consecutive steps of one branch as a group (a folder; nothing is changed or merged). It holds whole turns; a step is in one group at most. Group a multi-step analysis under a short name.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.group.create} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_group_create(viewer, from = "s4",
      name = "QC", to = "s9")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
